course: dictionary
lesson: 10665
title: Words about people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us how we feel about a person or a character. Unlikeable is one of them. Someone who is unlikeable is hard to like, because they are unkind, rude, selfish or unpleasant.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Feeling lonely at a new school does not mean you are unlikeable.» Being lonely is not the same as being unkind, so lonely people are not automatically unlikeable. Unlikeable describes how someone behaves.
explain: The second example shows the same idea. A girl is lonely, then finds friends, and the author says «she was never unlikeable, her friendships just hadn't had time or a place to grow». Ask yourself what the author wants you to think about her, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Unlikeable is an adjective, so it describes a person or a character.
fact: Unlikeable can also be spelled unlikable, and both spellings are correct.
fact: «An unlikeable hero» is a hero that readers find hard to like.
fact: «An unlikeable villain» is a villain that readers find unpleasant.
fact: Feeling lonely does not make someone unlikeable.
exercise: «Feeling lonely at a new school does not mean you are unlikeable.» What does unlikeable mean? | Brave and full of fun | Very clever and good at maths | Always alone and sad | *Hard to like because they are unkind, rude, selfish or unpleasant
exercise: A story has «an unlikeable villain». What does this tell the reader? | The villain is always singing happy songs | The villain lives in a castle by the sea | *The reader finds the villain hard to like | The reader wants to be the villain's best friend
exercise: Which other spelling of unlikeable is also correct? | *unlikable | unlike | unlikely | unfriendly
test: Read this: «she was never unlikeable, her friendships just hadn't had time or a place to grow.» Why did the author say she was never unlikeable? | She was rude to everyone in the art club | She was unpleasant to her teacher | She was selfish and never shared with anyone | *She was not unkind or rude; her friendships just needed time
test: Which word best describes a character who is rude, selfish and unkind to others? | Glum | Famished | Luminous | *Unlikeable
exam: Which sentence uses unlikeable correctly? | The unlikeable sky was blue and sunny all day. | The unlikeable dog ran across the park. | *The bully's cruel jokes made him very unlikeable. | She ate an unlikeable sandwich for lunch.
